      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T00:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Ganesh vs Graphite distinction is done via an enum in the C++ version:\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:tests/SkSLTest.cpp;l\u003d241;drc\u003d8aafaa3e4320343662ec525065fc4f5798af5257\n\nThe unit test name is `SkSL##name##_Ganesh` which gives that prefix/suffix but we only pass `#name` to the `test_ganesh` helper (same for Graphite).\n\nErrors are usually because I guessed the GL_RENDERER name wrong, or I scoped the test too tightly. The scopes aren\u0027t a perfect 1:1 mapping from go, since a lot of things are expressed slightly differently, e.g. `!b.extraConfig(\"Vulkan\")` is often used to mean OpenGL, but it could also match/disable in ANGLE or Metal, etc.",
